// Owner playtest row 24 at night: 23:00, 12x12 grid city, no traffic or parked cars. Re-aimed
// 2026-10-21 for main's rebuilt grid (divided viaduct at x = 0, ramp terminals at x = ±22; no
// unit passes the old x = -276.8 aim any more): patrol unit 2 drives north up x = -163.25. The
// racer (no heat) starts at (-164.9, 95) facing south, just over the centreline, cruises at
// 30 km/h from 1 s and meets it at 8.7 s: a front-corner clip (10 kN·s, 12 m/s closing) then a
// flank scrape. At night a pursuit otherwise needs a wanted racer within 40 m for 4 s; the hit
// unit recognises the racer at once instead, so wanted L2 and the pursuit start in the
// contact's tick. Without the fix this run has no police event for the racer at all; 0.3 m
// further right the unit dodges and there is no contact. Re-aim with
// `examples/probe_police.rs` if police spawning changes.
// Re-aimed for the road network centreline fix (playtest row 170): unit 2's patrol now comes
// up x = -163.25 about 270 m further south, so the racer starts at (-164.9, -190) on the same
// road: contact at 8.70 s (9.9 kN·s, 11.5 m/s closing), pursuit in the same tick. Starts at
// y = -185 … -230 hit it (contact 8.9 … 6.1 s); -180 hits too late for the 9.1 s limit.
// Police PR port (2026-10-24): aimed at one particular patrol unit, so like its day twin it
// keeps the patrol counts from before the owner's cut (`dense_patrols`, PR #64: one Core patrol
// at night, unit 2 no longer exists); it checks the assault rule, not how many cops patrol.
(
    name: "police_sideswipe_patrol_night",
    seed: 24,
    city: procedural(seed: 1, blocks_x: 12, blocks_y: 12, block_m: 110.0),
    time_of_day_h: 23.0,
    time_ratio: 1.0,
    mode: Simulation,
    parked_cars: false,
    traffic_density: 0.0,
    dense_patrols: true,
    assists: keyboard,
    entities: [
        (
            id: "racer",
            car: "debug_sedan",
            pos: (-164.9, -190.0, 0.0),
            yaw: 3.1416,
            driver: cruise(target_mps: 8.33, from_s: 1.0),
            inputs: [],
        ),
    ],
    duration_s: 11.0,
    hash_every: 24,
    expect: [
        speed_at(entity: "racer", t_s: 5.5, min: 7.5, max: 9.0),
        event_count(event: "Contact", entity: "racer", min: 1, max: 40),
        // Wanted-level change and pursuit within 0.4 s of the 8.7 s contact.
        police_event_before(kind: 2, t_s: 9.1),
        pursuit_started_before(t_s: 9.1),
    ],
)
